2.3 Application Principle

A fact may be OBSERVED without its cause being established. A mechanism may be REPORTED without confirmation by a primary source. A cause may be ESTABLISHED by the manufacturer and accepted by the regulator without an independent investigation having been conducted.

\boxed{\text{One status does not replace another}}

Methodological note on manufacturer investigations: Manufacturer investigations accepted by the FAA constitute the strongest publicly available evidence, yet they remain non-independent third-party analyses. This document therefore distinguishes "CAUSE ESTABLISHED (manufacturer + FAA acceptance)" from fully independent forensic findings.

Note on social media statements: Elon Musk's statements on X/Twitter are classified as REPORTED (manufacturer statement), not CAUSE ESTABLISHED, unless accompanied by a formal investigation closure. This applies to SN8, SN9, and SN11.

