3.2 Technical Glossary

Term Definition
Hard start Abnormal rocket engine ignition characterized by accumulation of unburned propellants in the combustion chamber, producing sudden overpressure upon ignition
Helium ingestion Introduction of helium bubbles into the propellant feed line, reducing fluid density and thus mass flow rate
Filter blockage Obstruction of a filter in the LOX feed line, reducing inlet pressure to turbopumps
Attic Non-pressurized zone between the LOX tank bottom and the aft heat shield
RVac Raptor Vacuum — Raptor engine version optimized for vacuum, with a wider nozzle
Soft splashdown Controlled contact with water, vehicle structurally intact and floating
Hard splashdown Contact with sufficient kinetic energy to cause significant damage or immediate destruction
COPV Composite Overwrapped Pressure Vessel
FTS Flight Termination System — commanded destruction mechanism
Ice clogging Formation of ice in propellant feed lines, potentially obstructing flow to engine inlets

